#######################################################################
#
# Suite A - Poisson disk error handling and reporting
#
# These tests feed deliberately BAD commands to
# createpts / poisson_disk and check that the failure is reported
# properly. Nothing here checks mesh numerics; that is Suite B.
#
#   sh run_error_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]
#
# Logs land in logs/. Exit status 0 means every test passed.
# Index of all the test suites: ../00README
#
#######################################################################
#
# WHY THERE ARE NO REFERENCE FILES
#
# The assertions are structural, not textual:
#
#   err*   at least one ERROR block, no crash
#   warn*  a WARNING block, no ERROR block, mesh still produced
#   all    every opened banner has a matching closing banner
#
# That means the suite keeps working when message wording changes,
# which matters because the wording is expected to keep improving.
# If you later want exact-text regression, capture logs/ as reference
# output once the messages settle.
#
# The balanced-banner check is the important one. In the ORIGINAL code
# five of seven error blocks and both warning blocks never emitted a
# closing banner, because each site hand rolled its own writloga
# sequence. Everything now routes through poi_log_block, which owns
# the format. If someone adds a message without going through it, this
# check fails.
#
#######################################################################
#
# FILES
#
# Polygon inputs, AVS UCD point sets:
#   unit_square.poly            convex baseline, 4 vertices
#   two_point.poly              2 vertices, too few
#   needle.poly                 min interior angle about 0.46 degrees
#   tilted_square.poly          not planar in X,Y
#   lshape_mid.poly             reflex corner at vertex 4
#   lshape_reflex_first.poly    reflex corner at vertex 1
#   lshape_reflex_last.poly     reflex corner at vertex 6
#
# The three L shapes are THE SAME SHAPE with the vertex list rotated.
# They must all behave identically. See warn02 below.
#
# h field control files:
#   hfield_too_small.mlgi       field at 0.1*h, below the 0.49*h floor
#   hfield_too_large.mlgi       field at 200*h, above the 100*h warn
#   hfield_vary_in_z.mlgi       3D, illegal values only away from the
#                               first z layer
#
#######################################################################
#
# TEST INDEX
#
# Parse phase
#   err01  bad dimension token            3d_bx
#   err02  command too short              missing tokens
#   err03  h wrong type                   token 5 is character
#   err04  h is zero
#   err05  h is negative
#   err06  bad connect token              2D, reported as token 7
#   err07  unknown option keyword         poison_seed
#   err08  option value wrong type        poisson_seed abc
#   err09  mesh object name numeric       token 3 is an integer
#   err10  THREE parse faults at once     accumulator test
#
# Geometry phase, 2D
#   err11  polygon has 2 vertices
#   err12  polygon edge shorter than h/2
#   err13  polygon angle below 9 degrees
#   err14  polygon not planar in X,Y
#   err15  h field below the 0.49*h floor
#
# 3D
#   err16  bad connect token              reported as token 6, not 7
#   err17  one missing POI_ box define
#   err18  THREE missing box defines      accumulator test
#   err19  h field illegal away from the first z layer
#
# Warnings, must NOT abort
#   warn01 nonconvex, reflex at vertex 4
#   warn02 nonconvex, reflex at vertex 1
#   warn03 nonconvex, reflex at vertex 6
#   warn04 h field above the 100*h warning threshold
#
#######################################################################
#
# TOKEN NUMBERS IN MESSAGES
#
# createpts_lg.f calls the drivers with imsgin(2), so the array the
# driver sees starts at the user's SECOND token. Messages add
# POI_TOKEN_OFFSET so the number printed matches what the user typed:
#
#     createpts / poisson_disk / 3d_box / mo_out / ...
#          1            2           3        4
#
# A bad dimension keyword is reported as token 3, not the internal 2.
#
#######################################################################
#
# THE FOUR TESTS THAT MATTER MOST
#
# err10 and err18
#   One command, several mistakes, ONE error block listing all of
#   them. The old code stopped at the first fault, so a command with
#   three mistakes took three edit-and-rerun cycles to diagnose. If
#   these ever report only one fault, the accumulator has regressed to
#   fail-fast.
#
#   Both decks carry two header lines the runner enforces:
#       # blocks   : 1
#       # contains : <text> | <text> | <text>
#   exactly one ERROR block, and every listed text inside it. Counted
#   on the deck's stdout only: stdout and lagrit.out carry the same
#   text, so the combined .all file shows every block twice (which is
#   why the other err* decks report "2 block/s"). Any deck may use
#   these two lines.
#
# warn02 and warn03
#   Regression tests for the test_convex corner coverage bug. The loop
#   ran i = 1, nnode-2 and each pass tested the turn at vertex i+1, so
#   the turns at vertex 1 and vertex nnode were never examined. A
#   polygon reflex at either of those vertices was reported CONVEX,
#   which skipped the warning AND the clipping pass and produced a
#   convex hull mesh that silently filled the concave notch.
#
#   warn01, warn02 and warn03 are the same L shape with the vertex
#   list rotated, so all three must warn and all three must produce
#   the same clipped outline. Under the old code warn01 warned and the
#   other two did not.
#
#######################################################################
#
# NOT COVERED HERE, AND WHY
#
# Dimension token mismatch against the driver actually called
#   poisson_disk_2d and poisson_disk_3d each verify that token 2
#   agrees with the driver. Going through createpts this is
#   unreachable, because the poisson_disk dispatcher routes on that
#   same token. The check exists for callers that invoke a driver
#   directly. Testable only by calling the drivers from Fortran.
#
# Error accumulator overflow
#   poi_err_report reports "and N further problems not shown" past
#   POI_ERR_MAX. Reaching 40 faults in one command needs about 20 bad
#   keyword pairs. Worth adding if the limit is ever lowered.
#
# dotaskx3d status
#   Still discarded at the single call site in poi_cmd, as it was at
#   all 65 original sites. A failing LaGriT command inside the driver
#   is not detected. Making those checked is its own change.
#
#######################################################################
